500603|Report Category|Asset Characteristics - Mutual Funds report is a generic report containing information regarding subscribed assets for Mutual Fund securities.A user will employ this report for many purposes,each of which are related to understanding characteristics regarding Mutual Fund assets.The data available in this report reflects information found on the 'Funds' tab in the Asset Information page.This report is not intended to be used for client/account investment in an asset or to manage the asset maintenance process|User|Read-Only|BOXI - Asset Characteristics - Mutual Funds
500603|Report Category|This is a generic report containing all performance related static data feed from SWP to Performance Station. A user will use this report for many purposes, each of which is related to understanding characteristics regarding account and communication group performance measurement flags and start or end dates. One of the key purposes of this report is to assist in the review of performance measurement dates.|User|Read-Only|Client Performance Measurement Characteristics Report
500603|Report Category|This is a generic report containing all income and interest information regarding held assets including asset with or without active positions. A user will use this report for many purposes, each of which is related to understanding characteristics regarding assets and how would these be reflected on client statements for a given end date. One of the key purposes of this report is to assist in the review of dividend amounts, coupon rates and yield rates.|User|Read-Only|BOXI - EAI Yield Characteristics Report
500603|Report Category|This report will provide fee variance by comparing periodic fee computation for date selections between the latest period and previous period.|User|Read-Only|BOXI - Periodic Fee Variance Report
500603|Report Category|The Asset Exposure Firms and Sub-Firms report is a generic report containing all information regarding an accounts holding across a users book of business. This report allows a user retrieve data at the Sub-Firm level. A user will use this report for many purposes, each of which are related to finding account holders based on search characteristics. The report runs for all the assets in the selected Firm or Sub-Firm and could result in a long delay in retrieving report data.|User|Read-Only|BOXI - Asset Exposure - Firms and Sub-Firms
