500572|Report Category|This is a generic report containing all income and interest information regarding held assets including asset with or without active positions. A user will use this report for many purposes, each of which is related to understanding characteristics regarding assets and how would these be reflected on client statements for a given end date. One of the key purposes of this report is to assist in the review of dividend amounts, coupon rates and yield rates.|User|Read-Only|BOXI - EAI Yield Characteristics Report
500572|Report Category|Asset Characteristics - Mutual Funds report is a generic report containing information regarding subscribed assets for Mutual Fund securities.A user will employ this report for many purposes,each of which are related to understanding characteristics regarding Mutual Fund assets.The data available in this report reflects information found on the 'Funds' tab in the Asset Information page.This report is not intended to be used for client/account investment in an asset or to manage the asset maintenance process|User|Read-Only|BOXI - Asset Characteristics - Mutual Funds
500572|Report Category|The Audit - Asset Characteristics report is used to identify securities which have had manual changes to one or more attributes within a user defined time period. It shows the old and new values, the date, time and name of the entity making the change.  Not applicable for ASP.|User|Read-Only|BOXI - Audit - Asset Characteristics Report
500572|Report Category|The ISA 14 Annual Statistical Return Boxi Report - provides ISA Managers with the information necessary to file their Stocks and Shares and Cash ISA Valuation of all amounts held under management in each specified type of qualifying investment in stocks and shares and cash ISAs.  Amounts on the Summary Report are rounded up to the nearest pound based on HMRC requirements. |User|Read-Only|BOXI - UK Tax HMRC ISA Plan Manager Reporting
500572|Report Category|The Fee Approval report can be used to review periodic fee computations and collection activities for a firm.  The report has four tabs, the first for account computation activity, the second has the related account collection activities, the third is for Fee Group Computation information and the forth tab has Fee Group Collection activity.|User|Read-Only|BOXI - Fee Approval Report
