500600|Report Category|The Account Characteristics report is a generic report containing all information regarding accounts.  A user will use this report for many purposes, each of which are related the understanding characteristics regarding accounts.  The report is not intended to be used for account holdings or valuations.|User|Read-Only|BOXI - Account Characteristics Report
500600|Report Category|The Corporate Actions Events Completed Report displays all CA event types that have been executed over a specified date period. The report is intended to be used by SEI Operations to monitor corporate action payments that have been made over a given period, and to compare the date the event was executed with the market announced Payable Date in order to validate service level standards.|User|Read-Only|BOXI - Corporate Action Events Report
500600|Report Category|The Fee Approval report can be used to review periodic fee computations and collection activities for a firm.  The report has four tabs, the first for account computation activity, the second has the related account collection activities, the third is for Fee Group Computation information and the forth tab has Fee Group Collection activity.|User|Read-Only|BOXI - Fee Approval Report
