500579|Report Category|The Investment Compliance (IC) Cross Reference Report was created to show a user the assignment details regarding firm level created IC rules. If an IC rule needs to be modified or deleted after it is has been assigned, this information helps the user understand the impact of the potential change.  A user may select one or more IC rule(s) and the IC Cross Reference Report displays details such as assignment level (i.e. all accounts, by servicing relationship, by account type, or by portfolio type).|User|Read-Only|BOXI - Investment Compliance Cross Reference Report
500579|Report Category|The Client Communication - Event Review Report provides details of Statement, Contract Note and Client Income and Disposal events set up on platform for a particular as of date. This report supports the ability to validate those events.|User|Read-Only|BOXI - Communication Events - Event Review Report
500579|Report Category|The Audit - 3rd Party Characteristics Report, is used to display changes to indicative data for third party entities on SWP.  Example: of Indicative data would be things such as names, titles, surnames, type of entity, address, address purpose, tax forms, etc.  This report also shows additions and deletions to 3rd party relationships such as statement recipient, communication recipient, trustee, tax beneficiary, etc.|User|Read-Only|BOXI - Audit - 3rd Party Characteristics
