500610|Report Category|The Investment Guideline drift report displays the number of  "in balance and out of balance" entities (which could be portfolio, account, client or portfolio, account groups) at the investment guideline level. This would enable users to monitor drift at the asset classification level. This report is scheduled to run once a day and will calculate the drift for all entities for which at least one investment guideline is associated.|User|Read-Only|BOXI - Investment Guideline Drift Summary Report
500610|Report Category|The Audit- Firm Level Overrides Report, is used to display any changes to universally traded securities that a firm may make to effect specific reporting for the firm. Examples of these changes would be a change to Long Description, Viewing Instrument Type, Country of Risk, etc.  Not applicable for ASP.|User|Read-Only|BOXI - Audit - Firm Level Asset Overrides
