500571|Report Category|The Asset Exposure Firms and Sub-Firms report is a generic report containing all information regarding an accounts holding across a users book of business. This report allows a user retrieve data at the Sub-Firm level. A user will use this report for many purposes, each of which are related to finding account holders based on search characteristics. The report runs for all the assets in the selected Firm or Sub-Firm and could result in a long delay in retrieving report data.|User|Read-Only|BOXI - Asset Exposure - Firms and Sub-Firms
500571|Report Category|This report includes fee rebates calculated, fee rebates calculated but not posted due to an exception and fee rebates calculated and have one-time fees generated as part of the final fee computation process for periodic fees computed in advance. The report displays information at the collection activity level (portfolio level). If there are multiple exceptions for a rebate computed record, then a single exception is listed in the 'Rebate not issued reason' column based on the priority order for exceptions.|User|Read-Only|BOXI- Final Fees Rebate for Advance Periodic Computations report
