500610|Report Category|The Investment Compliance (IC) Cross Reference Report was created to show a user the assignment details regarding firm level created IC rules. If an IC rule needs to be modified or deleted after it is has been assigned, this information helps the user understand the impact of the potential change.  A user may select one or more IC rule(s) and the IC Cross Reference Report displays details such as assignment level (i.e. all accounts, by servicing relationship, by account type, or by portfolio type).|User|Read-Only|BOXI - Investment Compliance Cross Reference Report
500610|Report Category|Intent of the report is to show the transactions that violated a particular Investment Compliance Rule and were overridden by a particular user. It should also display the Rule Name and Rule Type that caused the violation and the corresponding Accounts, and Portfolios. It should also display the Instrument and Transaction details along override details such as Overridden By, Overridden Date, and Override Reason of the person who overrode the violations. |User|Read-Only|BOXI - Investment Compliance Override Report
