500598|Report Category|The Asset Exposure Firms and Sub-Firms report is a generic report containing all information regarding an accounts holding across a users book of business. This report allows a user retrieve data at the Sub-Firm level. A user will use this report for many purposes, each of which are related to finding account holders based on search characteristics. The report runs for all the assets in the selected Firm or Sub-Firm and could result in a long delay in retrieving report data.|User|Read-Only|BOXI - Asset Exposure - Firms and Sub-Firms
500598|Report Category|Audit - Account Characteristics report displays changes to basic Account information over a specified date range. Changes are grouped by category and subcategory and highlight the Who, What, When, and How (Add, Modify, Delete) of the changes. The intent is to provide the user insight into intraday static data changes made to Account attributes to support audit controls.|User|Read-Only|NEW Name:  BOXI - Audit - Account Characteristics
500598|Report Category|This report is used to track the timeliness of market order executions. The report captures the elapsed time taken to execute the orders. The clock starts when the order is entered into GWP and stops when the order has been filled. The report will also display cancelled orders including limit orders as well as executed limit orders. This report may take several minutes to execute due to the volume and historical nature of this report.|User|Read-Only|BOXI - UK regulatory - Granular Timely Execution Report
