500615|Report Category|Audit - Account Characteristics report displays changes to basic Account information over a specified date range. Changes are grouped by category and subcategory and highlight the Who, What, When, and How (Add, Modify, Delete) of the changes. The intent is to provide the user insight into intraday static data changes made to Account attributes to support audit controls.|User|Read-Only|NEW Name:  BOXI - Audit - Account Characteristics
500615|Report Category|This report is used to track the timeliness of market order executions. The report captures the elapsed time taken to execute the orders. The clock starts when the order is entered into GWP and stops when the order has been filled. The report will also display cancelled orders including limit orders as well as executed limit orders. This report may take several minutes to execute due to the volume and historical nature of this report.|User|Read-Only|BOXI - UK regulatory - Granular Timely Execution Report
500615|Report Category|The Fee Approval report can be used to review periodic fee computations and collection activities for a firm.  The report has four tabs, the first for account computation activity, the second has the related account collection activities, the third is for Fee Group Computation information and the forth tab has Fee Group Collection activity.|User|Read-Only|BOXI - Fee Approval Report
500615|Report Category|The Fees and VAT report identifies transactions that are potentially value added tax (VAT) eligible for the purpose of verifying VAT was or was not correctly applied and reconciling the amounts collected to support remittance to HMRC on a periodic basis.|User|Read-Only|BOXI - VAT Charged Report
500615|Report Category|Client Communication Events - Summary provides all active Client Communication Events across a book of businesses and supports the ability to validate those Events.For each package selected, the package status, delivery method and other details are displayed, along with the total Events and then total Events split by Account, Client Communication Group and Client groups.|User|Read-Only|BOXI - Client Communication Events - Summary
500615|Report Category|Intent of the report is to show the transactions that violated a particular Investment Compliance Rule and were overridden by a particular user. It should also display the Rule Name and Rule Type that caused the violation and the corresponding Accounts, and Portfolios. It should also display the Instrument and Transaction details along override details such as Overridden By, Overridden Date, and Override Reason of the person who overrode the violations. |User|Read-Only|BOXI - Investment Compliance Override Report
500615|Document Type|DM Folder: Statements AFP Files (ID 130)|User|Read-Only|DM - Statements AFP Files (130)
500615|Report Category|This is a firm level report that identifies accounts that are not scheduled to receive a Communications Statement Event within the timeframe required by regulatory and, or Firm requirements. Exceptions are house accounts and accounts with no market value and transactions.|User|Read-Only|BOXI - Client Communication Event Exception
500615|Report Category|The Entitlement Review - User Definition Report lists characteristics about each user and the roles to which they have been assigned.  Only active users and role assignments are displayed.  This is not an audit trail of users, so once a user has been marked "Inactive", they no longer appear on the report.|User|Read-Only|BOXI - Entitlement Review - User Definition
500615|Report Category|The Client and Account Characteristics - Address Details report provides the contact information of Clients and their Account(s) including address and email. It is intended to be used by advisors, broker dealers and other parties to request contact information for their Clients so they may send communications (email and postal).|User|Read-Only|BOXI - Address Details
